{"id":"A2-L023","title":"Past Continuous: introduction","cefr":"A2","level":"A2","unit":"A2-U02","focus":"Past Continuous — introdução","targets":{"grammar":"Past Continuous — introdução","pron":"Schwa /ə/","verbs":["stop"],"pv":["find out"],"expr":[],"words":["blackout","power line","match","horizon","lantern","headlamp","resident","nobody","fall","gale","power cut","dark street","fallen tree","candle light","board game","radio news"],"field":"Compras","genre":"Editorial / opinião","skill":"Leitura","words_min":16},"frames":[{"tag":"Abertura","title":"Lesson 23 · Past Continuous: introduction","blocks":[{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Nesta aula","body":["**Foco:** Past Continuous — introdução.","**Verbos:** stop.","**Phrasal verbs:** find out.","**Pronúncia:** Schwa /ə/.","**16 palavras novas** (compras).","**Texto do dia:** editorial / opinião."]},{"type":"p","t":"**Objetivo de comunicação (A2):** eu consigo dizer o que estava acontecendo no passado e usar find out."},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Ponte para as provas","body":["Você começa a praticar tarefas curtas no formato das provas.","Esta aula treina **ler textos curtos e achar informação (IELTS Reading, TOEFL Reading)**."]}]},{"tag":"Aquecimento","title":"Warm-up · Say the words","blocks":[{"type":"p","t":"Toque em 🔊, ouça e repita cada palavra. Depois tente adivinhar o sentido."},{"type":"words","items":[["blackout","apagão"],["power line","linha de energia"],["match","partida"],["horizon","horizonte"],["lantern","lampião"],["headlamp","lanterna de cabeça"],["resident","morador"],["nobody","ninguém"],["fall","cair"],["gale","ventania"],["power cut","power cut"],["dark street","dark street"],["fallen tree","fallen tree"],["candle light","candle light"],["board game","board game"],["radio news","radio news"]]}]},{"tag":"Leitura","title":"Reading · An editorial","blocks":[{"type":"text","title":"What Were You Doing?","paras":["When the lights went out last Tuesday, people were doing very different things. Some were **cooking**, some were **watching** a match, and a few were **sleeping**.","Neighbors **stopped** talking and **were looking** at the sky. We **found out** later: a tree fell on a power line. That night, nobody was using a phone, and everyone was talking."],"kicker":"OPINION","by":"Neighborhood Voice","gloss":[["power line","linha de energia"],["match","partida"],["sky","céu"],["nobody","ninguém"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"People were cooking when the lights went out.","ans":"T","why":"some were cooking."},{"q":"Everyone was using a phone.","ans":"F","why":"nobody was using a phone."},{"q":"A tree fell on a power line.","ans":"T","why":"tree fell."}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“power line” = ?","opts":["linha de energia","linha de ônibus","fila"],"ans":0,"why":"power line."},{"q":"“nobody” means…","opts":["ninguém","todos","alguém"],"ans":0,"why":"nobody."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"Past Continuous","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Forma","Exemplo"],"rows":[["was/were + -ing","**I was cooking.**"],["negativa","**We weren’t sleeping.**"],["pergunta","**Were you watching TV?**"],["resposta curta","**Yes, I was. / No, I wasn’t.**"]],"cap":"Past Continuous"},{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Regra","body":"Usamos para ações **em progresso** num momento do passado: *At nine, I was cooking.*"}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences","bank":null,"items":[{"s":"I ___ dinner at nine. (cook)","a":"was cooking","why":"was + -ing."},{"s":"They ___ a match. (watch)","a":"were watching","why":"were + -ing."},{"s":"We ___ . (not sleep)","a":"weren’t sleeping","why":"neg."},{"s":"We ___ out later. (find)","a":"found","why":"find out.","say":"We found out"}]},{"type":"match","title":"Match the word to its meaning","pairs":[["blackout","apagão"],["power line","linha de energia"],["match","partida"],["horizon","horizonte"],["lantern","lampião"]]},{"type":"order","title":"Put the words in order","items":[{"words":["was","cooking","I"],"ans":"I was cooking","pt":"Eu estava cozinhando."},{"words":["alone","Were","you"],"ans":"Were you alone","pt":"Estava sozinho?"}]}]},{"tag":"Vocabulário","title":"Words and expressions","blocks":[{"type":"vocab","items":[{"w":"blackout","pos":"word","pt":"apagão","ex":"A city blackout.","expt":"Um apagão na cidade."},{"w":"power line","pos":"word","pt":"linha de energia","ex":"A fallen power line.","expt":"Uma linha de energia caída."},{"w":"match","pos":"word","pt":"partida","ex":"A football match.","expt":"Uma partida de futebol."},{"w":"horizon","pos":"word","pt":"horizonte","ex":"The horizon was dark.","expt":"O horizonte estava escuro."},{"w":"lantern","pos":"word","pt":"lampião","ex":"A small lantern.","expt":"Um lampião pequeno."},{"w":"headlamp","pos":"word","pt":"lanterna de cabeça","ex":"A strong headlamp.","expt":"Uma lanterna de cabeça forte."},{"w":"resident","pos":"word","pt":"morador","ex":"A new resident.","expt":"Um novo morador."},{"w":"nobody","pos":"word","pt":"ninguém","ex":"Nobody called.","expt":"Ninguém ligou."},{"w":"fall","pos":"word","pt":"cair","ex":"Leaves fall.","expt":"As folhas caem."},{"w":"gale","pos":"word","pt":"ventania","ex":"A strong gale.","expt":"Uma ventania forte."},{"w":"power cut","pos":"word","pt":"power cut","ex":"falta de luz","expt":"A power cut."},{"w":"dark street","pos":"word","pt":"dark street","ex":"rua escura","expt":"A dark street."},{"w":"fallen tree","pos":"word","pt":"fallen tree","ex":"árvore caída","expt":"A fallen tree."},{"w":"candle light","pos":"word","pt":"candle light","ex":"luz de vela","expt":"Candle light."},{"w":"board game","pos":"word","pt":"board game","ex":"jogo de tabuleiro","expt":"A board game."},{"w":"radio news","pos":"word","pt":"radio news","ex":"notícias do rádio","expt":"Radio news."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"culture","t":"Expressões desta aula","body":["**I was cooking.** — Eu estava cozinhando.","**Were you alone?** — Estava sozinho?","**No, my neighbors were talking outside.** — Não, meus vizinhos conversavam lá fora.","**Kind of.** — Meio que.","**More or less.** — Mais ou menos.","**As usual.** — Como sempre.","**As I said…** — Como eu disse…"]}]},{"tag":"Verbos","title":"Verbs in focus","blocks":[{"type":"verbs","items":[{"v":"stop","pt":"parar","forms":[["I / you / we / they stop","I stop here."],["he / she / it stops","She stops now."]]}]},{"type":"table","head":["Phrasal verb","Significado","Exemplo"],"rows":[["**find out**","descobrir","We found out later. — Descobrimos depois."]],"cap":"Phrasal verbs"}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"During the blackout","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"During the blackout","lines":[["Ana","What were you doing when the lights went out?","O que você fazia quando a luz acabou?"],["Leo","I was cooking.","Eu estava cozinhando."],["Ana","Were you alone?","Estava sozinho?"],["Leo","No, my neighbors were talking outside.","Não, meus vizinhos conversavam lá fora."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: Schwa /ə/","items":[{"label":"Schwa /ə/","note":"Vogais fracas viram /ə/: about, banana, today, the.","words":["about","banana","today","family","another"]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Say what you were doing at nine last night.","pt":"Diga.","model":"I was watching TV."},{"q":"Ask: What were you doing?","pt":"Pergunte.","model":"What were you doing?"},{"q":"Say what people weren’t doing.","pt":"Diga.","model":"Nobody was using a phone."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write 5 sentences with the Past Continuous.","model":"I was cooking when the lights went out. My neighbors were talking outside. We weren’t using phones. The children were laughing. Nobody was sleeping.","checklist":["Usei **was/were + -ing**","Usei **uma negativa**","Usei **when**"],"words":"5 frases"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note","blocks":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Check yourself","items":[{"q":"What does “blackout” mean?","opts":["apagão","linha de energia","horizonte"],"ans":0,"why":"**blackout** = apagão."},{"q":"What does “power line” mean?","opts":["partida","linha de energia","lampião"],"ans":1,"why":"**power line** = linha de energia."},{"q":"What does “match” mean?","opts":["horizonte","lanterna de cabeça","partida"],"ans":2,"why":"**match** = partida."},{"q":"What does “horizon” mean?","opts":["horizonte","lampião","morador"],"ans":0,"why":"**horizon** = horizonte."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Estratégia para as provas","body":["Treine esta habilidade com o formato de tarefas curtas das provas (TOEFL/IELTS).","Leia o enunciado primeiro e procure as palavras-chave."]},{"type":"box","kind":"teach","t":"Nota para o futuro professor","body":["Use exemplos reais da vida dos alunos e peça frases próprias.","Corrija o erro mais frequente da aula em grupo, sem expor o aluno.","Retome o conteúdo na aula seguinte com um exercício curto."]}]}]}